[
  {
    "layout_id": "page-0:text-1",
    "page_id": 0,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.135,
      0.217,
      0.692,
      0.817
    ],
    "text": "Electronic Fuel Injection By Dr.S.John Alexis",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-1:text-1",
    "page_id": 1,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.069,
      0.066,
      0.381,
      0.946
    ],
    "text": "A modern gasoline injection system uses pressure from an electric fuel pump to spray fuel into the engine intake manifold.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-2:text-1",
    "page_id": 2,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.067,
      0.067,
      0.279,
      0.942
    ],
    "text": "Like a carburetor, it must provide the engine with the correct air-fuel mixture for specific operating conditions.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-2:text-2",
    "page_id": 2,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.352,
      0.067,
      0.564,
      0.946
    ],
    "text": "Unlike a carburetor, however,PRESSURE,not engine vacuum,is used to feed fuel into the engine.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-2:text-3",
    "page_id": 2,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.633,
      0.067,
      0.776,
      0.933
    ],
    "text": "This makes the gasoline injection system very efficient",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-3:text-1",
    "page_id": 3,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.057,
      0.026,
      0.262,
      0.97
    ],
    "text": "A gasoline injection system has several possible advantages over a carburetor type of fuel system.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-3:text-2",
    "page_id": 3,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.286,
      0.027,
      0.347,
      0.653
    ],
    "text": "Some advantages are as follows:",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-3:text-3",
    "page_id": 3,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.364,
      0.028,
      0.546,
      0.97
    ],
    "text": "\\* Improved atomization. Fuel is forced into the intake manifold under pressure that helps break fuel droplets into a fine mist.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-3:text-4",
    "page_id": 3,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.564,
      0.031,
      0.694,
      0.968
    ],
    "text": "\\* Better fuel distribution. Equal flow offuel vapors into each cylinder.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-3:text-5",
    "page_id": 3,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.71,
      0.028,
      0.901,
      0.971
    ],
    "text": "\\* Smoother idle. Lean fuel mixture can be used without rough idle because of better fuel distribution and lowspeed atomization.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-4:text-1",
    "page_id": 4,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.074,
      0.055,
      0.196,
      0.944
    ],
    "text": "\\* Lower emissions. Lean efficient air-fuel mixture reduces exhaust pollution.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-4:text-2",
    "page_id": 4,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.211,
      0.055,
      0.392,
      0.944
    ],
    "text": "\\* Better cold weather drivability. Injection provides better control ofmixture enrichment thana carburetor.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-4:text-3",
    "page_id": 4,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.411,
      0.055,
      0.593,
      0.945
    ],
    "text": "\\* Increased engine power. Precise metering of fuel to each cylinder and increased air flow can result in more horsepower output.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-4:text-4",
    "page_id": 4,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.611,
      0.054,
      0.793,
      0.945
    ],
    "text": "\\* Fewer parts. Simpler， late model，electronic fuel injection system have fewer parts than modern computer-controlled carburetors.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-5:text-1",
    "page_id": 5,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.118,
      0.053,
      0.267,
      0.917
    ],
    "text": "There are many types of gasoline injection systems.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-5:text-2",
    "page_id": 5,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.3,
      0.08,
      0.359,
      0.886
    ],
    "text": "A basic knowledge of the different classifications :",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-5:text-3",
    "page_id": 5,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.385,
      0.265,
      0.444,
      0.795
    ],
    "text": "\\* single- or multi-point injection",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-5:text-4",
    "page_id": 5,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.461,
      0.266,
      0.539,
      0.735
    ],
    "text": "\\* indirect or direct injection",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-1",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.09,
      0.053,
      0.149,
      0.697
    ],
    "text": "Single and Multipoint EFl Systems",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-2",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.197,
      0.053,
      0.241,
      0.645
    ],
    "text": "Fuel injection systems classifiedby point of injection.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-3",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.277,
      0.053,
      0.321,
      0.734
    ],
    "text": "Single Point Fuel Injection (Throttle Body Injection-TBl)",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-4",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.333,
      0.053,
      0.456,
      0.304
    ],
    "text": "Injectorlocated inside throttlebody,sitson topof inletmanifold.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-5",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.494,
      0.053,
      0.616,
      0.236
    ],
    "text": "Injectorsprays fuel fromabove throttlevalve.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:text-6",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.652,
      0.053,
      0.737,
      0.246
    ],
    "text": "ECUcontrols injectoropening.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-6:figure-7",
    "page_id": 6,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_6_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.385,
      0.339,
      0.842,
      0.917
    ],
    "text": "Inletmanifold",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:text-1",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.111,
      0.062,
      0.171,
      0.707
    ],
    "text": "Single and Multipoint EFl Systems",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:text-2",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.22,
      0.062,
      0.262,
      0.359
    ],
    "text": "Multipoint Fuel Injection",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:text-3",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.274,
      0.061,
      0.397,
      0.335
    ],
    "text": "Injectorlocatedineach branchof inletmanifold, belowthrottlevalve.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:text-4",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.465,
      0.061,
      0.55,
      0.315
    ],
    "text": "Injectorsspray fuel directly into each port.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:text-5",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.618,
      0.062,
      0.703,
      0.295
    ],
    "text": "ECU controls opening of injectors.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-7:figure-6",
    "page_id": 7,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_7_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.338,
      0.335,
      0.817,
      0.938
    ],
    "text": "Inletmanifold",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-8:figure-1",
    "page_id": 8,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_8_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.065,
      0.049,
      0.862,
      0.953
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-9:text-1",
    "page_id": 9,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.032,
      0.016,
      0.137,
      0.959
    ],
    "text": "A multi-point injection system, also called port injection, has an injector in the port (air-fuel passage) going to each cylinder.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-9:text-2",
    "page_id": 9,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.192,
      0.016,
      0.348,
      0.96
    ],
    "text": "Gasoline is sprayed into each intake port and toward each intake valve.Thereby, the term multipoint (more than one location) fuel injection is used.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-9:text-3",
    "page_id": 9,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.355,
      0.359,
      0.39,
      0.761
    ],
    "text": "Multipoint fuel injection (MPI)",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-9:figure-4",
    "page_id": 9,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_9_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.392,
      0.363,
      0.996,
      0.951
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-10:figure-1",
    "page_id": 10,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_10_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.055,
      0.042,
      0.932,
      0.941
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-11:text-1",
    "page_id": 11,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.039,
      0.114,
      0.104,
      0.519
    ],
    "text": "Electronic Injectors",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-11:text-2",
    "page_id": 11,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.14,
      0.001,
      0.321,
      0.993
    ],
    "text": "The injectors can survive the excessive temperature and pressure of combustion by using the fuel that passes through it as a coolant",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-11:figure-3",
    "page_id": 11,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_11_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.343,
      0.298,
      0.88,
      0.962
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:text-1",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.045,
      0.002,
      0.35,
      0.488
    ],
    "text": "An indirect injection system sprays fuel into the engine intake manifold. Most gasoline injection systems are of this type.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:text-2",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.361,
      0.001,
      0.633,
      0.485
    ],
    "text": "Direct injection forces fuel into the engine combustion chambers. Diesel injection systems are direct type.",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:text-3",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.652,
      0.005,
      0.798,
      0.433
    ],
    "text": "So Gasoline electronic Direct Injection System",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:figure-4",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_12_Figure_0.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.019,
      0.614,
      0.329,
      0.963
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:figure-5",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "figure",
    "asset_ref": "assets/_page_12_Figure_1.jpg",
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.345,
      0.61,
      0.727,
      0.964
    ],
    "text": "",
    "source_type": "image"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-12:text-6",
    "page_id": 12,
    "layout_type": "text",
    "asset_ref": null,
    "bbox_norm": [
      0.81,
      0.001,
      0.869,
      0.903
    ],
    "text": "is Classified as : multi-point and Direct injection systems",
    "source_type": "text"
  },
  {
    "layout_id": "page-13:text-1",
